# CR 121.5: combat damage to a Battle removes defense counters -- the same
# CounterType-specific branch dealPermanentDamage already has for a
# planeswalker's loyalty (combat-attack-a-planeswalker), but a distinct
# `if t.Has(cardtype.Battle)` case, not shared code (combatdamage.go).
# queue battleprotector answers assignBattleProtector, asked unconditionally
# for any Battle with no protector yet, before startturn's own first
# state-based-action check ever gets to see it. The protector must be an
# opponent of the Battle's own controller (ai here) -- naming the controller
# itself leaves assignBattleProtector's own selfProtector case true, which
# asks again on every subsequent state-based-action check.
queue battleprotector human
startturn human
advance 5
queue attackers 1
queue attacktarget 2
declareattackers
advance
queue blocks none
declareblockers
advance
advance
combatdamage
